    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is clean, additive, and consistent with the existing codebase idioms:\n\n- The new `public static int fiscalYear(LocalDate)` is the right shared unit: it captures the one non-trivial rule (the 1-July boundary) in a single place and is reused by all three consumers \u2014 `getFiscalYear()`, `getTenureFiscalYears()`, and `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`. This eliminates the duplication that would otherwise arise from each site re-deriving the fiscal year, and the previous inline `.getYear() % 100` in `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` is correctly replaced by a call to it.\n- Placing fiscal-year derivation on `Owner` matches the existing altitude: `Owner` already hosts derived-at-response-time getters (`getMembershipPoints`, `getMembershipLevel`, `getHouseholdSize`, `getLocality`) and a public static domain helper (`regionOf`), so `fiscalYear` / `getFiscalYear` sit naturally alongside them rather than turning the class into a new catch-all.\n- `getTenureFiscalYears()` cleanly supersedes `getTenureDays()` (private, same shape, same null/negative guard via `Math.max`), and the unused `ChronoUnit` import is correctly removed.\n- `getFiscalYear()` follows the established derived-getter pattern (null-safe, documents \"not persisted\"), and the callers/docs (`getMembershipPoints` Javadoc, `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` Javadoc, and the OpenAPI schema) are all updated coherently with the behaviour change.\n\nThe only borderline point is that the \"last two digits, zero-padded\" idiom (`fiscalYear(...) % 100` with `%02d`) appears in both `getFiscalYear()` and `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`, but they emit different final formats (`FY<YY>` vs `<code>-M<YY>`) and the meaningful shared logic already lives in `fiscalYear()`, so further extraction would be over-engineering. A maintainer would find this natural.",
